DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection in h2o HTTP server. The server must be
  started with BOTH --exec-mode AND --exec-verbose for the vulnerable /exec
  endpoint to be reachable. A URL query parameter flows through an snprintf
  buffer into system(). A pipe-character filter can be bypassed with semicolon.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — struct, two flags):
  mechanism:  Two CLI flags (--exec-mode, --exec-verbose) stored in global
              struct { int enabled; int verbose; } exec_cfg
  check:      `exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.verbose` guard in exec_handler_on_req
              and in register_exec_handler (handler not registered if gate fails)
  complexity: one struct, two integer flags, both required simultaneously

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — snprintf buffer):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  req->path (set by HTTP parser)
  path:       exec_handler_on_req() extracts substring after "cmd=" via memcmp/offset
              cmd is copied into a stack-allocated char cmd_buf[4096] via snprintf
              cmd_buf is passed directly to system()
  transforms: snprintf("%.*s") — copies but does not interpret the string

SANITIZATION (S2 — pipe blocked):
  check:      linear scan for '|' character; returns 400 if found
  bypass:     use semicolon (;) instead of pipe to chain commands
              e.g. cmd=id>/tmp/marker works; cmd=id|tee /tmp/marker is blocked

SINK:        system(cmd_buf) in exec_handler_on_req() (src/main.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/main.c — 5 hunks:
    1. globals:            added exec_cfg struct and exec_handler_on_req() function
                           and register_exec_handler() after cmd_argc/cmd_argv
    2. longopts[]:         added --exec-mode (E) and --exec-verbose (V) entries
    3. optstring:          changed "c:m:tvh" to "c:m:tvhEV"
    4. option dispatch:    added case 'E' and case 'V' to set exec_cfg fields
    5. post-config:        register_exec_handler() called after configurator_apply
                           only when both flags are set

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./h2o -c h2o.conf --exec-mode --exec-verbose
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18086/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting either --exec-mode or --exec-verbose causes the handler
               to never be registered; /exec returns 404

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's inherited stderr, not the HTTP response.
    Use a write-to-file payload to confirm blind RCE.
  - The snprintf buffer is 4096 bytes; payloads longer than ~4090 chars are
    silently truncated (I2 characteristic).
  - Pipe character (|) in cmd returns HTTP 400; use semicolon (;) to chain.
